@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Security & Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-8">
        <div class="inventory-card p-4 p-md-5">
            <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-3 mb-4">
                <div class="brand-icon" style="width: 52px; height: 52px; font-size: 1.6rem;">
                    <i class="bi bi-shield-lock-fill"></i>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-0">System Security & State Architecture</h3>
                    <span class="text-muted small">Small Business Retail Data Governance</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h5 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-2">1. State Management & Session Lifecycle</h5>
            <p class="text-secondary small mb-3">
                This application utilizes <code>HttpContext.Session</code> to maintain temporary operational state:
            </p>
            <ul class="text-secondary small mb-4">
                <li><strong>Session Action Counter:</strong> Tracks the number of catalog, stock, and supplier operations executed within the active session.</li>
                <li><strong>Last Action Timestamp:</strong> Stores the most recent inventory modification timestamp to assist staff with shift audit handovers.</li>
                <li><strong>Restock Order Draft:</strong> Preserves non-committed purchase requisition items in memory until verified and finalized.</li>
            </ul>

            <h5 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-2">2. Database & Data Integrity</h5>
            <p class="text-secondary small mb-3">
                All permanent data is persisted using Entity Framework Core through the <code>Pomelo.EntityFrameworkCore.MySql</code> provider. Foreign key constraints enforce relationship integrity:
            </p>
            <ul class="text-secondary small mb-4">
                <li>Categories and Suppliers cannot be deleted if products are actively linked to them, preventing orphaned records.</li>
                <li>Every Stock In and Stock Out movement logs an immutable transaction record with staff attribution.</li>
            </ul>

            <h5 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-2">3. Model Validation & Sanitization</h5>
            <p class="text-secondary small mb-0">
                All incoming input is verified both client-side via jQuery Validation Unobtrusive and server-side via .NET DataAnnotations (<code>[Required]</code>, <code>[Range]</code>, <code>[StringLength]</code>, <code>[RegularExpression]</code>) alongside Anti-Forgery token validation (CSRF defense).
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
